{"id": "30c66a22-fb46-4bb3-bfed-ca7815c7d2d4", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I see the latest minor version in the 15 line is 15.19, with 17.9 as default, and I should flag the Aurora PG 15 support lifecycle as something to verify rather than assert outright. I'm also noting that the cluster's MultiAZ flag being false doesn't necessarily mean it isn't multi-AZ for Aurora, since that field only turns true when readers exist in another AZ—I should check the cluster's AvailabilityZones list instead.

Backups look healthy with a 7-day retention and active PITR, well within Aurora's 35-day max, so no action needed there. The bigger concern is that the reader instance sits in the same AZ as the writer (us-east-1d)—if that AZ fails, both go down simultaneously, and recovery would require spinning up a new instance in a different AZ since I can't directly move an existing instance's AZ; I should surface this as a recommendation to create a reader in us-east-1b or 1c.

